IO-06: read every token on an input line, not just the first 40

getTokens() stores at most MAXTOKS tokens per line and drops the rest of the
line without a message. MAXTOKS was 40, so a [CURVES] or [TIMESERIES] line
with more than 19 pairs, or a [TRANSECTS] GR line with more than 19 stations,
lost its later values. MAXTOKS is now MAXLINE/2 (512), the most tokens that
fit in the 1023 characters getTokens() is given, so no token of a line that
is read can be dropped. Lines with 40 tokens or fewer are parsed exactly as
before; getTokens() now clears 512 token pointers per line instead of 40.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-06_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/consts.h b/src/legacy/engine/consts.h
index 23d0701..56beedf 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/consts.h
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/consts.h
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
  * \def MAXTOKS
  * \brief Maximum number of items per line of input
  */
-#define MAXTOKS 40 // Max. items per line of input
+#define MAXTOKS (MAXLINE/2) // Max. items per line of input (all that fit in a line)
 
